speechtext:
I doubt whether they would have the same effect. Much depends upon the significance that is attached to a particular policy that is undertaken. Governments
[Mr. Blackmore.}
have always been in the habit of borrowing money for specific purposes. But when a government departs entirely from the view that it must use money secured by loans or taxation for public purposes, and prints an addition to the dominion note issue for that purpose, I believe that it tends, rightly or wrongly, to destroy the confidence of the people in a more or less stable purchasing power of the national currency.
